  data: {
    LLM: 'Each betting turn, the active player stakes between table minimum and current pot size. Dealer reveals a card. If the player can show a card in hand of the same suit and higher rank, the player wins an equal amount from pot; otherwise the stake is lost to pot. If pot empties mid-deal, remaining players do not bet and deal passes left.',
    Player: 'Each betting turn, the active player stakes between table minimum and current pot size. Dealer reveals a card. If the player can show a card in hand of the same suit and higher rank, the player wins an equal amount from pot; otherwise the stake is lost to pot. If pot empties mid-deal, remaining players do not bet and deal passes left.',
    objective: "Win bets from the bank by proving a same-suit higher card against the dealer's turned-up card.",
    gameplay: 'Each betting turn, the active player stakes between table minimum and current pot size. Dealer reveals a card. If the player can show a card in hand of the same suit and higher rank, the player wins an equal amount from pot; otherwise the stake is lost to pot. If pot empties mid-deal, remaining players do not bet and deal passes left.',
    keyRules: [
      'Dealer alone funds the initial pot in Shoot.',
      'Players are dealt only three cards each.',
      'Pot exhaustion immediately ends remaining bets for that deal.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '3 to about 8 players, with one acting as dealer/banker.',
      deck: '52-card deck, ace high.',
      equipment: 'Cards and money/chips for a shared dealer-controlled pot.',
      dealing: 'Dealer stakes the pot, then deals 3 cards to each non-dealer player. Players look at cards only just before their own bet.',
    },
    turnFlow: 'Each betting turn, the active player stakes between table minimum and current pot size. Dealer reveals a card. If the player can show a card in hand of the same suit and higher rank, the player wins an equal amount from pot; otherwise the stake is lost to pot. If pot empties mid-deal, remaining players do not bet and deal passes left.',
