      'Setup example: 3 card(s) per player.',
      "Rule example: Win bets from the bank by proving a same-suit higher card against the dealer's turned-up card.",
      'Turn-flow example: Each betting turn, the active player stakes between table minimum and current pot size. Dealer reveals a card. If the player can show a card in hand of the same suit and higher rank, the player wins an equal amount from pot; otherwise the stake is lost to pot. If pot empties mid-deal, remaining players do not bet and deal passes left.',
      'Scoring example: Shoot is bankroll-based: successful bets pay from pot, failed bets feed the pot, and deal rotation depends on pot survival or bust. Session winner is the player/dealer position with best net profit under agreed stop condition..',
